{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1556611-storytelling-a-rant","id":1556611,"title":"Storytelling a Rant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-14T09:52:42-08:00","id":1556611,"title":"Storytelling a Rant","content":"This weekend, my players will be in the middle of a pretty big Anarch Rant (This is an Anarch thing in my WoD, not exclusively Brujah). Since it's Brooklyn, there are between 50 to 60 Anarchs showing up. I certainly won't give every single one a voice, but I think it should be social contests between spokespeople for each Anarch Crew. That drops it down to about 11 spokespeople and independents, along with my 4 PCs.<br /> <br /> I'm considering adapting the Social Conflict rolls from <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i>, as laid out in <i>The Danse Macabre</i>. Has anyone used those in the past? I'm especially curious if you've adapted them to V5 (the rules we use).<br /> <br /> As far as prep, I am thinking of having each crew have a set opinion about the main events leading up to the rant (a combination of Brooklyn attempting to break free from a single New York City Prince and said Prince (Qadir, following the events of <i>Reckoning of New York</i>) trying to reestablish dominance over the city after the last year was spent recovering from the hunter attack on Elysium and the feud with Vritra), particular beefs with other crews, and a primary goal.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have tips for huge social events where the players are just one part of a bigger picture? I feel like I will do just fine come the game, but I love hearing how other people would have handled it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T22:36:14-08:00","id":1556702,"title":"","content":"Eleven is far too many; that is just creating work for yourself for marginal or no benefit. You will struggle to create distinct voices, or individual viewpoints, or characters that can be distinguished by the players.<br /> <br /> Have twenty characters at the Rant, with three distinct viewpoints being promoted. Have NPCs approach the PCs to obtain support for these viewpoints as a set of social interactions. Have consequences for each of the three viewpoints, and then the viewpoint supported by the players (or the majority of the players) being the one that prevails. If the Anarchs are about to try to kill the Prince, the players should be the ones to set them on this course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}